Henry J Cobb <hcobb@io.com> writes:

> Rogues should start with their daggers in quiver rather than secondary
> weapon slot.

With beginning rogues, I normally separate the dagger stack so that I
wield one of them as primary weapon, another one as secondary, and quiver
the rest. Of course, they must be individually named to keep them
separated: I #name the primary one as "w" (for wielding), secondary one as
"2" and the stack of the remaingin ones as "q" (for quiver).

Then when I do melee combat, I alternate between just hitting with the
primary dagger and #twoweaponing, depending on what I fight because the
beginning character often hits better with a single weapon.

> New players would be much better served with the daggers as missile
> weapons rather than attempt unskilled twoweapon.

True. But I still think practising the twoweapon skill against newts, grid
bugs and other easy monsters is also a good idea for rogues and some other
classes.

